      ],
      "title": "Official excess-alliance counting rule remains unresolved; adopted table case is playable",
      "finding": "Printed p33 directs equal newly exhausted Army pieces or as many as possible and calls non-equality a successful Crisis. Printed p22 treats alliances as temporary Army pieces with printed strength used once for a single purpose. The official aid uses comparative attacker/defender strength with defender winning ties and names exhausted local alliances in defender strength. This supports the user’s successful-defense reading, but the retained primary sources provide no explicit whole-piece overshoot/counting example or instruction reconciling the p33 non-equality language. Army-piece status alone does not prove how excess is counted. The source set therefore cannot independently establish the official outcome or a general >= rule.",
